cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Assay: an open, reproducible framework for evaluating AI artifacts"
message: >-
  If you use this software in academic work, please cite it using
  the metadata below.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "TheRandomDev9"
repository-code: "https://github.com/metahub-ai/assay"
url: "https://github.com/metahub-ai/assay"
abstract: >-
  Assay evaluates AI artifacts — skills, MCP servers, agents and plugins —
  in two tiers. A static tier of deterministic checks reads the artifact's
  manifest, documentation and file contents. An opt-in behavioral tier runs
  the artifact inside a sandbox, driven by one model and graded by another,
  with a deterministic safety scan over the captured commands. Every check
  declares a determinism tier, every score reports its own coverage, and
  every transcript is recorded so a verdict can be re-derived by someone who
  does not trust the party that produced it.
keywords:
  - AI safety
  - software supply chain
  - Model Context Protocol
  - agent skills
  - LLM-as-judge
  - reproducibility
  - static analysis
  - dynamic analysis
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.2.4
